                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "39fb81f7-3a7f-3b49-87ca-677b04e98dfc",
                        "entry_id": "11a849de-7eb7-3a08-bcbe-c2927ac689f7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To astound; to paralyse, to stun."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "eb2cf6fd-3611-4664-a8ee-98a1f29fc0cb",
                                "sense_id": "39fb81f7-3a7f-3b49-87ca-677b04e98dfc",
                                "text": "thenne Brastias sawe his felawe ferd so with al / he smote the duke with a spere that hors & man fell doune / that sawe kyng Claryaunce and retorned vnto Brastias / and eyther smote other soo that hors & man wente to the erthe / and so they lay long astonyed / & their hors knees brast to the hard bone"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "86c16d03-e860-4f44-b046-75afcbdcbf87",
                                "sense_id": "39fb81f7-3a7f-3b49-87ca-677b04e98dfc",
                                "text": "And it cam to passe, that when Jesus had ended these saynges, the peple were astonnied at his doctryne."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d438b452-a111-4068-8659-ce44362da401",
                                "sense_id": "39fb81f7-3a7f-3b49-87ca-677b04e98dfc",
                                "text": "Verily the violence of a griefe, being extreme, must needs astonie the mind, and hinder the liberty of her actions."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7e714347-27ca-41ee-997a-79f37d77e600",
                                "sense_id": "39fb81f7-3a7f-3b49-87ca-677b04e98dfc",
                                "text": "On th' other ſide, Adam, ſoon as he heard / The fatal Treſpaſs don by Eve, amaz'd, / Aſtonied ſtood and Blank, vvhile horror chill / Ran through his veins, and all his joynts relax'd; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a3d0081-9e23-430d-b2f2-acab16128af8",
                                "sense_id": "39fb81f7-3a7f-3b49-87ca-677b04e98dfc",
                                "text": "Upright men shall be astonied at this […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "42167633-50ec-4bc7-bd41-4616754c7aff",
                                "sense_id": "39fb81f7-3a7f-3b49-87ca-677b04e98dfc",
                                "text": "When some Beloveds, 'neath whose eye / The sweet lids lay lights of my childhood, one by one / Did leave me dark before the natural sun, / And I astonied fell and could not pray […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
